1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Zhao Ming of Shang''' - From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
2 CONT
2 CONT According to the ancient writings, '''Zhao Ming''' (Chinese: 昭明; pinyin: Zhāo Míng; ? – ?) was a Chinese nobleman and an ancestor of the Shang dynasty.[1] His family name was '''Zi''' (子).
2 CONT
2 CONT His father was Xie of Shang, born in Shangqiu (商丘), Henan (河南). Among the twelve ancestors of the King Tang of Shang, Zhao Ming was the second-generation king of the Shang Kingdom.
2 CONT
2 CONT After the death of Xie, Zhao Ming inherited the throne and expanded the spread of civilization. After his death, his son Xiang Tu succeeded to the throne.
2 CONT
2 CONT Source: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Zhao_Ming_of_Shang
