1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''The 43rd Generation Ancestor: 譚國 (Tán Guó)'''
2 CONT
2 CONT He was also called 譚瓊 (Tán Qióng).
2 CONT
2 CONT His name was changed to 姬孝公 (Jī Xiào Gōng).
2 CONT
2 CONT "Those 姒 (Sì) people who living in Tan County at the beginning were using Tan as their surname instead of using Sì. That's why some people say Tan and Si clan has a same ancestor. Finally, Emperor Mu of Zhou Dynasty 周穆王 (Zhōu Mù W
2 CONC áng) also conferred 竹 (Zhú)'s [Tan (早) brother, they were sent to be farmers in Zhangqiu County 章丘縣 (Zhāng Qiū Xiàn) of the Shangdong Province. However, 竹 (Zhú)'s [Tan (早)] brother changed their surname to 譚 (Tán) when they settle
2 CONC d in Tan County. They were part of the Tan Clan.  譚 (Tán), 姒 (Sì) and 早 (Tan) join together, share weal and woe and make their history together. These three clans sharing their days for more than three hundred years, they had been
2 CONC  joined. Therefore, that's the history of Tan, which was founded in the Zhou Dynasty. [The saying that Tan clan was originated from the Zhou Dynasty was wrong.]
2 CONT
2 CONT So Tan County is the origin of the Tan Clan."
