1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''The 52nd Ancestor: 月可 (Yuè Kě)''' 
2 CONT
2 CONT He was born in 863 BC, during the Xizhou (两周) Dynasty. He was the governor of the Tan vassal county. His tomb was located at the east of 對面嶺 (Duì Miàn Lǐng), 周 (Zhōu) Village.
2 CONT
2 CONT His wife, Ms. Zi, had two sons named 草彬 (Cǎo Bīn) and 草立 (Cǎo Lì ), and two daughters. She was buried at the south of 博山嶺 (Bó Shān Lǐng).
