2 CONT He was born in 806 BC, during the Xizhou Dynasty. He succeeded to the governor of the Tan vassal county. His tomb is located at the north of 昆侖山 (Kūn Lún Shān). 
2 CONT
2 CONT His wife, 陳 (Chén), had two sons named 花喬 (Huā Qiáo) and 花桂 (Huā Guì) and two daughters. She is buried at the east of Duimiangling 王舍 (Wáng Shě).
