2 CONT He was born in 775 BC, the early days of 東周 (Dōng Zhōu) Dynasty. He succeeded to the governor of the Tan vassal county. His tomb was located at the south of Duimingling, left side of 車山店 (Chēs Hān Diàn) with his wife.
2 CONT
2 CONT His wife, 田 (Tián) had two sons named 開來 (Kāi Lái), 開進 (Kāi Jìn), and a daughter.
