2 CONT King Zhuangxiang of Qin (281– 6 July 247 BCE[2]), personal name Ying Yiren, Ying Ziyi or Ying Zichu, was a king of the Qin state.[3] He was the father and predecessor of Qin Shi Huang, who would later unify China proper and become
2 CONC  China's first emperor. He was posthumously honored as Taishang Huang by the Qin dynasty.
